  "question_type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ be non-zero vectors such that $|\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}| = |\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}|$. Then the angle between $\\vec{a}$ and $\\vec{b}$ is:",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "$|\\vec{a} + \\vec{b}|^2 = |\\vec{a} - \\vec{b}|^2$<br /><br />$\\Rightarrow 2|\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\cos\\theta = -2|\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\cos\\theta$<br /><br />$\\Rightarrow 4|\\vec{a}||\\vec{b}|\\cos\\theta=0$<br /><br />$\\Rightarrow \\cos\\theta=0 \\implies \\theta=90^\\circ$<br /><br />Correct option: C.",
